      {
        "thread_id": "TH5",
        "thread_goal": "Review pilot feedback and decide on adjustments before scaling.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M71",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hello everyone, the pilot is complete and I've gathered the participant feedback from the survey (T9). I've compiled the results into the draft 'Feedback & Impact Evaluation Report', which you can find at A6. The general sentiment was positive.",
            "mentions": [
              45680,
              4784,
              89425,
              605
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "tada",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M72",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M71",
            "text": "Great news. I've just read through A6. The positive comments on the de-escalation role-plays are fantastic. A recurring piece of constructive feedback seems to be that the micro-break exercises felt a bit 'sudden' and some people were hesitant to join in at first.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M73",
            "speaker_id": 89425,
            "reply_to": "M72",
            "text": "That's valuable feedback and makes perfect sense. For the next wave, I suggest we add a dedicated 5-minute segment at the very beginning of the first session. I can use it to explain the 'why' behind the breaks, demonstrate all the movements, and create a more comfortable environment. Normalizing the activity is key.",
            "mentions": [
              45680
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M74",
            "speaker_id": 4784,
            "reply_to": "M71",
            "text": "My team said they enjoyed the sessions. They found the tips useful.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M75",
            "speaker_id": 605,
            "reply_to": "M71",
            "text": "The response rate for the survey was 88%, which is great! I'm already starting to update the main program documents with these results.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M76",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M73",
            "text": "That's a brilliant and simple fix, @89425. I think that will make a huge difference. Another point from A6 was that the 'Active Listening' module felt a bit theoretical to some. Maybe we can shorten the theory part and add another short role-play there?",
            "mentions": [
              89425
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M77",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": "M76",
            "text": "So, are we proposing two main changes? A better intro for the wellbeing part, and making the listening module more practical?",
            "mentions": [
              45680
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M78",
            "speaker_id": 605,
            "reply_to": "M77",
            "text": "What about the third module, 'Setting Boundaries'? The feedback on that was good, right?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M79",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M78",
            "text": "Yes, feedback on that was very strong. People found it immediately applicable. So I think we should keep that one as is.",
            "mentions": [
              605
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M80",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M77",
            "text": "Exactly. So to summarize the decision for our path forward: \n1. KEEP: The 'De-escalation' and 'Setting Boundaries' modules.\n2. CHANGE: Add a 5-min practical intro for the wellbeing exercises. Also, revise the 'Active Listening' module to be more interactive and less theoretical.\n3. DROP: Nothing, the core content is solid. \n\nDoes everyone agree with this plan before we scale?",
            "mentions": [
              56723,
              4784,
              89425,
              605
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D9"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M81",
            "speaker_id": 89425,
            "reply_to": "M80",
            "text": "I fully support this. The adjustment for the wellbeing part is a clear improvement.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M82",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": "M80",
            "text": "This sounds like a sensible plan based on the data. I agree.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M83",
